From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Giuseppe Maggio <jertlok@proton.me>
Date: Sat, 12 Sep 2026 01:58:23 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] misc: fpc1020: add a bring-up-only app_id override

request_firmware(qcom/msm8998/taimen/fpctzappfingerprint.mdt) fails
reproducibly with -ELOOP on real hardware, from inside
kernel_read_file_from_path_initns() -- but the identical inode opens
cleanly through every userspace path tried (plain open, O_NOFOLLOW,
/proc/1/root) and a fresh hardlink to the same inode fails identically,
so it is neither a permissions problem nor a broken symlink at the
directory level. cmnlib.mdt, loaded by the exact same function one call
earlier, succeeds. Root cause not found tonight; see
bringup/fpc-tee-chardev-test/ for the full diagnostic trail. This blocks
the real, production load path -- decision 1 in this file's header
comment stands, and a fresh boot still needs it fixed.

The trustlet is already resident this boot (app_id 196611, loaded
earlier by bringup/qseecom-app-load.c), so app_id= lets bring-up skip
straight to it -- INIT is still sent -- and the chardev, GET_FPC_INFO
and fprintd could all be exercised tonight despite the open firmware
bug. Loudly marked BRING-UP ONLY: production has no way to know this id
in advance.

Signed-off-by: Giuseppe Maggio <jertlok@proton.me>
---
 drivers/misc/fpc1020.c | 31 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 30 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/misc/fpc1020.c b/drivers/misc/fpc1020.c
index c02feb73decf..a05ffba676f4 100644
--- a/drivers/misc/fpc1020.c
+++ b/drivers/misc/fpc1020.c
@@ -162,6 +162,23 @@ struct fpc1020_image {
 	size_t total_len;
 };
 
+/*
+ * BRING-UP ONLY, not a production interface: request_firmware() for
+ * FPC1020_TZ_APP_NAME reproducibly fails with -ELOOP on the device this
+ * was first tested on, root cause not yet found (the same inode opens
+ * fine through every userspace path tried, including a fresh hardlink and
+ * /proc/1/root -- see bringup/fpc-tee-chardev-test/ for the diagnostic
+ * trail). Since the trustlet was already loaded resident by an earlier
+ * probe this boot, this parameter lets bring-up skip straight to that
+ * known app id -- INIT is still sent -- so the chardev, GET_FPC_INFO and
+ * fprintd can be exercised without waiting on the firmware-loading bug.
+ * A production boot has no way to know this id in advance (see decision
+ * 1 in this file's header comment) and must go through the real load.
+ */
+static unsigned int app_id_override;
+module_param_named(app_id, app_id_override, uint, 0444);
+MODULE_PARM_DESC(app_id, "BRING-UP ONLY: skip the trustlet/cmnlib load and use this already-resident app id instead (0 = load normally)");
+
 struct fpc1020 {
 	struct device *dev;
 	struct gpio_desc *reset_gpio;
@@ -457,6 +474,16 @@ static int fpc1020_bring_up_locked(struct fpc1020 *fpc1020)
 
 	lockdep_assert_held(&fpc1020->lock);
 
+	if (app_id_override) {
+		dev_warn(fpc1020->dev,
+			"app_id=%u module param set -- skipping trustlet/cmnlib "
+			"load, sending straight to that already-resident id "
+			"(BRING-UP ONLY, see the param's own comment)\n",
+			app_id_override);
+		fpc1020->app_id = app_id_override;
+		goto send_init;
+	}
+
 	ret = qcom_scm_qseecom_app_region_notify(FPC1020_TZ_REGION_ADDR,
 						 FPC1020_TZ_REGION_SIZE);
 	if (ret)
@@ -493,7 +520,8 @@ static int fpc1020_bring_up_locked(struct fpc1020 *fpc1020)
 		 * trustlet is already resident from an earlier bind this
 		 * boot, QSEOS_APP_START refuses to start it again -- and
 		 * there is no way to recover that earlier id (see the file
-		 * header, decision 1). Only a reboot clears this.
+		 * header, decision 1). Only a reboot clears this -- or, for
+		 * bring-up, the app_id= module param above.
 		 */
 		return dev_err_probe(fpc1020->dev, ret,
 				     "app_load(%s) failed -- if this trustlet "
@@ -502,6 +530,7 @@ static int fpc1020_bring_up_locked(struct fpc1020 *fpc1020)
 				     FPC1020_TZ_APP_NAME);
 	}
 
+send_init:
 	ret = fpc1020_tz_send_locked(fpc1020, FPC1020_TZ_GRP_SENSOR,
 				     FPC1020_TZ_CMD_INIT);
 	if (ret)
